<title>FRANCE: U.S. principal destination for April 97 Paris exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. principal destination for April 97 Paris exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in April 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris ADP, figures show.</p>
<p>April 1997  export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 47,718 tonnes, an increase of 2.3 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris ADP, figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 top destinations by country for ADP exports in April 1997, with percentage change on April 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p> Destinations	 tonnes  Percent vs</p>
<p>				    April '96</p>
<p> 1. United States   10,531  down  3.2</p>
<p> 2. Japan		2,485  down  5.9</p>
<p> 3. Hong Kong	  2,131    up 18.5</p>
<p> 4. Germany	    2,071  down 26.5</p>
<p> 5. Canada	     1,697  down  3.2</p>
<p> 6. UK		   1,344  down  7.1</p>
<p> 7. U.A.E.	     1,331    up  6.9</p>
<p> 8. Mexico	     1,108    up 42.1</p>
<p> 9. India		1,103    up  7.5</p>
<p>10. Brazil	     1,008  down 22.5</p>
<p>11. Fr.W.Indies	  998    up  9.2</p>
<p>12. Reunion		894    up 18.8</p>
<p>13. Singapore	    791    up 22.8</p>
<p>14. Saudia Arabia	759  down 29.1</p>
<p>15. Egypt		  749  down  0.1</p>
<p>16. Italy		  688  down 14.7</p>
<p>17  Lebanon		675    up 10.5</p>
<p>18. China		  540  down 20.8</p>
<p>19. Thailand	     535  down  7.7</p>
<p>20. Argentine	    496    up  6.6</p>
